    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that `POST /api/owners` default `registrationDate` to the server's current date when none is supplied, and always return it in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format. There's a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`) with 2 tests \u2014 both now pass, along with the full build.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it's both an accepted input on create and returned on the `Owner` output. The OpenAPI generator regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` with a `LocalDate registrationDate` (same treatment as the existing `birthDate` field).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after mapping, default the date to `LocalDate.now()` when the client didn't supply one; a supplied date is kept as-is.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests use hsqldb; the others were updated for consistency.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` picks up `registrationDate` automatically since the property names match on both the DTO\u2194entity mappings, so no mapper change was needed. Jackson serializes `LocalDate` to the ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` string the spec asks for.\n\nResult: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
